While the <a href="https://www.macrumors.com/2026/09/09/apple-announces-foldable-iphone-duo/">iPhone Duo</a> is the first foldable iPhone ever and has some unique features like Duo FaceTime and <a href="https://www.macrumors.com/2026/09/09/apple-pencil-usb-c-iphone-duo/">forthcoming Apple Pencil support</a>, the device lacks some other features available on the <a href="https://www.macrumors.com/2026/09/09/apple-announces-iphone-18-pro-and-iphone-18-pro-max/">iPhone 18 Pro and iPhone 18 Pro Max</a>.<br/>
<br/>
<img src="https://images.macrumors.com/article-new/2026/09/iphone-duo-hero.jpg" alt="" width="1600" height="899" class="aligncenter size-full wp-image-1063424" /><br/>
Below, we have listed 10 features that are missing on the iPhone Duo:<br/>
<br/>
<ul><li>A dedicated <strong>Telephoto camera</strong> with up to 8× optical zoom. Instead, the iPhone Duo's main 48-megapixel Fusion camera has "optical-quality" 2× zoom.</li><br/>
	<li><strong>Variable aperture</strong> for the main 48-megapixel Fusion camera, which provides greater control over depth of field in photos and videos.</li><br/>
	<li>A higher-resolution <strong>18-megapixel Center Stage front camera</strong>. On the iPhone Duo, this camera is 12 megapixels.</li><br/>
	<li><strong>Action button</strong>.</li><br/>
	<li><strong>Face ID</strong>. Instead, the iPhone Duo has a Touch ID button.</li><br/>
	<li><strong>LiDAR Scanner</strong>, which measures depth for augmented reality purposes.</li><br/>
	<li>Other camera features: <strong>Pro controls</strong> in the Camera app, <strong>ProRAW</strong>, <strong>ProRes RAW</strong>, <strong>spatial photos and videos</strong>, and more.</li></ul><br/>
